From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 11:09:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: run dynamic IFC by default on shared LRO rings

Dynamic IFC steers the TCP flows of listed local applications to an
LRO ring. The vendor code left it off until user space enabled it,
and gave a ring to four sessions only. A session started only when
the application sent, and two vendor components wrote the LRO
aggregation limit of the ethernet driver.

Dynamic IFC now starts when its IFC module loads, and stops when
that module or the hook module goes away. A session without a ring
slot shares an LRO ring, and the ring set follows the device tree.
Ring 12 is the last slot, because it shares its interrupt with the
TX completions. An application that only receives gets a session
too. The ethernet driver is the only writer of the aggregation
limit, so the agg_num command and the lro_agg_num line leave both
proc files. bbst is in the default application list.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
